  "table_name": "campaign",
  "description": "Salesforce Campaign object — one row per Campaign record from the SOQL query. The API returns paginated page envelopes (totalSize/done/nextRecordsUrl/records); records are extracted from each page's 'records' array and flattened. attributes.type/url carry SObject metadata. Standard fields cover core campaign attributes, financial metrics, member counts, and hierarchy rollup fields. Hierarchy rollup fields (Hierarchy*) aggregate values across the campaign hierarchy. Total* fields are additional hierarchy-level rollups. MCAE/Pardot fields (TotalEmailsDelivered, UniqueEmail*, TotalForm*, TotalLandingPage* and their Hierarchy equivalents) are feature-gated and only populated when Marketing Cloud Account Engagement is enabled. Custom fields (suffix _c) are org-specific extensions covering event logistics, call tracking, and EquiTrust-specific fields. Parent.Name is resolved via SOQL relationship traversal from ParentId.",
